14. Scenario-based interview questions
These are especially useful for someone with real backend development experience.
- [ ] An API takes five seconds to respond. How would you debug it?
- [ ] An API works in Postman but fails from the frontend. What would you check?
- [ ] Your application suddenly starts returning HTTP 500. How would you investigate?
- [ ] A database query is slow. How would you identify the bottleneck?
- [ ] Your application sends duplicate emails. How would you prevent this?
- [ ] Two users update the same record simultaneously. How would you handle it?
- [ ] A transaction updates one table but fails before updating another. What should happen?
- [ ] Redis contains outdated data. How would you fix it?
- [ ] A downstream service is unavailable. How should your API behave?
- [ ] A Kafka consumer processes the same message twice. How would you handle it?
- [ ] Your application runs out of database connections. What would you inspect?
- [ ] A scheduled job runs twice across multiple application instances. How would you prevent duplicate execution?
- [ ] An endpoint should be accessible only to administrators. How would you implement this?
- [ ] How would you implement pagination for millions of records?
- [ ] How would you prevent a user from placing the same order twice?
- [ ] How would you design a centralized exception-handling mechanism?
- [ ] How would you safely deploy a database schema change?
- [ ] How would you debug a bean creation or dependency injection failure?
- [ ] How would you investigate a LazyInitializationException?
- [ ] How would you troubleshoot an unexpected transaction commit or rollback?
